Cross-file consistency audit of nfmcd_impl/experiments/*.csv and *.log
Read-only audit, no models fitted, no nf_mcd/* touched. Scope excludes
compound_results.csv, sigtest_results.csv, and anything under a
data/<newdataset>/ dir, which were owned by other jobs running at audit time.

=====================================================================
(A) CONFIRMED CONSISTENT
=====================================================================

A1. Plain-default NFMCD() results (crisismmd, fakeddit, dblp, amazon; seeds
    0-2) agree to 6 decimal places on onmi/modularity/f1 across every file
    that reports them:
      baselines_results.csv (method=nfmcd_full)
      clusterer_results.csv (method=default)
      variant_results.csv   (variant=default, graph=orig)
      robust_refresh_results.csv (method=nfmcd_default, group=orig)
      mnar_results.csv      (method=nfmcd_full, scheme=mcar_control, p=0.00)
      missing_results.csv   (method=nfmcd_full, mode=none, p=0.00)
    21 (dataset, seed) groups checked across >=2 sources each, 0 mismatches.
    Example (crisismmd, seed 0): onmi=0.590905, modularity=0.519782,
    f1=0.757263 in all six files.

    Note: variant_results.csv also stores a 'rewired50' graph variant under
    the SAME variant='default' label, disambiguated by its 'graph' column.
    An audit query that forgets to filter graph=='orig' will see large
    apparent "mismatches" (e.g. onmi 0.591 vs 0.289) -- these are not a bug,
    they're the documented edge-rewiring robustness check from earlier in
    the project. Filtering correctly resolves it. (I hit this myself on the
    first pass -- noting it in case anyone else audits this data later.)

A2. fakeddit_real_lcc's community count (k_used=6) agrees across
    missing_results.csv, mnar_results.csv, realgraph_results.csv,
    robust_refresh_results.csv for every k-taking method. The k_used=21
    values that also appear in these files belong exclusively to Louvain
    (base:louvain / louvain rows), which picks its own community count --
    already documented project-wide as expected behavior for
    Louvain/DEMON/SLPA. Confirmed by direct row inspection, not just
    inference.

A3. DBLP/Amazon overlap ground truth is cited identically everywhere it
    appears: DBLP 1072 nodes, 11/1072 (1.03%) true overlap; Amazon 146
    nodes, 68/146 (46.58%) true overlap (overlap_results.csv, part B rows).

A4. kselect_results.csv's claimed ONMI-vs-k peaks were independently
    recomputed from the raw data and match exactly: crisismmd peaks at
    k=7 (0.609), fakeddit at k=6 (0.423, not k_true=10), fakeddit_real_lcc
    still rising at k=13 (0.145) at the edge of the search window, dblp at
    k=8 (0.670), amazon at k=2 (0.839, not k_true=4).

A5. rank_results.csv's claimed "ONMI rises with pca_rank_div, flattening
    around 16-32" was independently recomputed (common_dim=8, crisismmd +
    fakeddit only -- PHEME is text-only and correctly excluded, since the
    CCA rank cap cannot affect a dataset with no image modality to align):
    div2=0.168, div4=0.459, div8=0.576, div16=0.735, div32=0.734, div64=0.755.
    Exact match to the previously reported table. Monotonic apart from the
    div16->div32 dip of 0.001, which is noise, not a violation.

A6. overlap2_results.csv's blend_strength=0.0 "sanity check" rows were
    independently compared against the original overlap_results.csv Part A
    run (a separate experiment, run earlier, using different code paths for
    the same underlying computation). Mean AUROC by overlap rate matches
    exactly: r0.1=0.483, r0.2=0.503, r0.3=0.530, r0.4=0.498 in both files.
    This is a strong independent confirmation, not just a self-reported claim.

A7. The documented CCA-overfit/rank-cap relationship between
    experiments/rank_summary.log and CLAUDE.md's "robust preset" section is
    substantively correct: clusterer_results.csv's fcmad|raw rows (the
    pre-rank16 preset) really do differ from current NFMCD.robust() output
    by a real, non-trivial margin -- e.g. crisismmd seed 0: 0.6735 (stale)
    vs 0.7067 (current robust_refresh_results.csv) -- consistent with the
    ~0.03-0.13 gap already reported to the user.

=====================================================================
(B) EXPECTED DIVERGENCE (differs, but for a known/documented reason)
=====================================================================

B1. clusterer_results.csv's fcmad|raw rows vs. current NFMCD.robust()
    output differ because NFMCD.robust() gained pca_rank_div=16 (and later
    vectorized_fusion=True, verified bit-identical so it does not
    contribute to this gap) after clusterer_results.csv was generated.
    Documented in CLAUDE.md ("fcmad|raw rows ... used the default cap, so
    they no longer match the preset"). Confirmed real and correctly flagged
    -- see C1 below for one inaccuracy in exactly how CLAUDE.md describes
    which files this applies to.

B2. tuning_results.csv vs. tuning_results_v1.csv, explain_results.csv vs.
    explain_results_v1.csv, nbr_explain_results.csv vs.
    nbr_explain_results_v1_tv_only.csv are each pairs of a superseded run
    and its replacement, already disambiguated by an explicit _v1 suffix at
    creation time (not something later re-labeled) -- no reader could
    mistake one for the other. No action needed.

=====================================================================
(C) UNEXPLAINED DISCREPANCIES / DOCUMENTATION ERRORS
=====================================================================

ONE finding, minor, documentation-only (not a numeric bug in any result):

C1. CLAUDE.md (the "robust preset" note) states: "The fcmad|raw rows in
    clusterer_results.csv and rank_results.csv predate pca_rank_div=16 and
    are stale for the preset." This is only half true. clusterer_results.csv
    genuinely contains fcmad|raw rows (confirmed stale, see B1/A7).
    rank_results.csv does NOT contain any method matching "fcmad" or a raw-
    content label at all -- I enumerated its 53 unique method values
    directly and none contain "fcmad" or "raw". rank_results.csv uses an
    entirely different, already-current naming scheme (nf|r<div>|c<dim>)
    introduced fresh for that experiment; it was never stale in the first
    place, so there is nothing in it to discount. This doesn't invalidate
    any reported number (rank_results.csv's own numbers are fine and
    already independently re-verified in A5/A7), but CLAUDE.md's file
    reference is factually wrong and could send someone hunting for a
    "stale" row in rank_results.csv that isn't there. Low severity --
    recommend just dropping "and rank_results.csv" from that CLAUDE.md
    sentence.

No other unexplained discrepancies were found across ~24 cross-file
comparisons, 3 independent recomputations of summarized claims, and one
independent re-derivation of a headline number (overlap2's blend=0 check).

=====================================================================
(D) STALE FILES
=====================================================================

D1. clusterer_results.csv's fcmad|raw rows -- stale, documented (B1/C1).
D2. tuning_results_v1.csv, explain_results_v1.csv,
    nbr_explain_results_v1_tv_only.csv -- superseded, self-evidently
    labeled by filename, no separate warning needed.
D3. Nothing else found stale. rank_results.csv is NOT stale (see C1) --
    correcting the implication in CLAUDE.md's current wording.

Could not verify from this machine whether the published results webpage
(an HTML artifact in Claude's scratchpad, not part of this repo) reflects
the current robust-preset numbers or an earlier snapshot -- that file isn't
reachable from this filesystem audit.

=====================================================================
Comparisons made: ~24 cross-file numeric matches (21 default-config groups
+ k_used check + overlap ground truth + 3 recomputed summary claims +
1 independent re-derivation). Passed: all of them, after one self-corrected
query bug (A1 note). Findings: 1 minor documentation inaccuracy (C1), no
numeric bugs found.
